Package: os7-backup
Version: @OS7_VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Bastian Wirth <bastian.wirth@upinblue.com>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: os7-module (= @OS7_VERSION@), sanoid, procps, openssh-client
Homepage: https://github.com/upinblue/os7
Description: OS/7 backup — snapshot policy, replication and verification
 The units and scripts behind Enable-OS7Backup, Start-OS7Backup and
 Get-OS7BackupStatus: a first-boot unit that establishes the policy and a timer
 that replicates to the configured targets.
 .
 THE SNAPSHOTTING AND THE REPLICATION ARE SANOID'S AND SYNCOID'S, wrapped and
 never reimplemented. What OS/7 adds is which datasets, which targets, and
 whether it actually worked — because both tools report success in cases where
 nothing happened. sanoid exits 0 after a failed zfs snapshot, and its
 --monitor-snapshots answers from a cache deliberately allowed to be five hours
 old. So the status cmdlet asks ZFS, on the source and over ssh on the target,
 and never asks either tool.
 .
 procps is here because `ps` is an undeclared dependency of both programs:
 sanoid's lock check and syncoid's "is the target already receiving" check both
 run it, and neither the package's Depends nor its documentation says so.
